config MTK_MT5725_WLS_SUPPORT
	bool "Maxic MT5725 wireless charger (Doogee S88 Pro, from the disassembly)"
	depends on MTK_CHARGER
	select WTK_USB_INSERT_DETECT
	default n
	help
	  Maxic MT5725 wireless charger of the Doogee S88 Pro (E977),
	  reconstructed by reading the disassembled factory kernel. The factory
	  config turns it on (CONFIG_MTK_MT5725_WLS_SUPPORT=y) and no public tree
	  has the source: without this symbol `olddefconfig` silently discards the
	  factory config line and the driver never enters the kernel.

	  THE `select` IS NOT A CONVENIENCE.  `mt5725.c` calls `usb_insert_online`,
	  which lives in another translation unit of which this project has
	  reconstructed ONE function out of five: without it the kernel link stops
	  with "undefined reference to `usb_insert_online'".  Measured -- it is the
	  fifth of the six symbols the first `LD vmlinux` ever attempted asked for.
